Subject: [PATCH 0/3] hexagonrpcd: Pixel 4a (sunfish) ADSP sensor bring-up
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

These three patches make hexagonrpcd serve the sensor bring-up FastRPC
traffic the Pixel 4a (sunfish) ADSP needs, so the SEE/CHRE sensor firmware
comes up on mainline Linux. They apply on top of upstream linux-msm/hexagonrpc
commit 23a6964 ("tools: make json-c optional").

Together they take the sunfish sensor stack from "ADSP crashes on boot" to
accelerometer/ALS/proximity working end to end (KWin auto-rotation, iio-
sensor-proxy). The port that uses them lives at
github.com/miromraz/mobian-pixel4a-port; the built binary and library are not
committed there, so build this series and drop them into the image.

  1. ADSP sensor-registry support for Pixel 4a (sunfish) -- serves the
     sensor registry tree (config + per-sensor registry entries) the SEE
     framework reads over the apps_std/hexagonfs endpoints, so the sensor
     firmware finds its calibration and platform config instead of faulting.

  2. fix heap overflow in apps_std_stat in-place path -- the in-place stat
     path wrote past the caller's buffer; caught with ASan while the ADSP
     hammered stat() during registry enumeration. Correctness/safety fix.

  3. serve sns_registry platform values (raw sysfs format) -- exposes the
     platform registry values in the raw sysfs format the sensor firmware
     expects, completing the registry the ADSP consults at bring-up.

miromraz (3):
  hexagonrpcd: ADSP sensor-registry support for Pixel 4a (sunfish)
  hexagonrpcd: fix heap overflow in apps_std_stat in-place path
  hexagonrpcd: serve sns_registry platform values (raw sysfs format)

